# Clinical Trial Data Validation Using SAS

## Project Overview

This is a self-directed project created to practice Clinical SAS and Clinical Data Management concepts using fictional clinical-trial-style datasets.
The project focuses on importing clinical data into SAS, performing data-quality checks, identifying discrepancies, and checking consistency between related datasets.

## Tools Used

* SAS 9.4 / SAS Studio
* Base SAS
* DATA Step
* PROC SQL
* PROC SORT
* PROC IMPORT
* PROC CONTENTS
* PROC PRINT

## Datasets

| Dataset | Purpose                                   |
| ------- | ----------------------------------------- |
| DEMOG   | Subject-level demographic information     |
| VITALS  | Vital signs collected during study visits |
| LABS    | Laboratory test results                   |
| AE      | Adverse-event information                 |
| VISIT   | Study visit information                   |

## Validation Checks

The project includes checks for:

* Missing values
* Invalid values
* Duplicate records
* Invalid dates
* Invalid visit and status values
* Unmatched subjects
* Subject and visit consistency across datasets

## Cross-Dataset Validation
PROC SQL was used to compare subjects and visit information between datasets.

Examples include:

* VITALS → DEMOG
* LABS → DEMOG
* AE → DEMOG
* VISIT → DEMOG
* VITALS → VISIT
* LABS → VISIT
* AE → VISIT

## Key Learning
During the project, I also identified and corrected issues in my own validation logic, including SQL join logic and character-to-date conversion.
This helped me understand that validation programs themselves need to be tested before findings are treated as true discrepancies.

## Project Outputs
The project includes SAS validation programs, fictional datasets, validation findings, and project documentation.

## Important Note
This is a self-directed educational project using fictional data. It does not represent experience with a real clinical trial, sponsor, CRO, or real patient data.
